I hear this a lot and I used to think it  makes some sense, but I don't 
anymore.  The last two characters that should have ascended (one did ascend 
and one died on my stash level to prove to me that I do indeed need a ring of 
free action) both of them were easy and boring Before the castle.  One of them 
(the one that died) used one wish adn the other used none, but both of them 
had a full kit.  There was probably only a week between those two characters 
so it's not as if they just both had extraordinary luck.  It's just that if a 
character is going to be really uber then it can be really uber with or 
without a wand of wishing unless you get rather unlucky.  If you don't 
polypile then that would make a difference, but that's a conduct, so that's 
different.  Wishes aren't what make the game boring, they're what help me 
spend less time waiting around and looking for the things I don't have.  The 
character who died and shouldn't have didn't have gloves of dex (or any other 
special gloves and he didn't have a t-shirt or  a special helm, but it didn't 
matter really.  If I'd wanted to, I might have wished for some piece of the 
ascension kit, but even if I didn't it wouldn't have made the game less 
boring, because I know that by the time that character got all the way down 
and back up he would have been an easy ride.  Wishing isn't the problem.  The 
problem is that the game finishes before the end.  

